From 50533a7251bf304d8c3744b8c2b6e6b77c8dff2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabio Valentini <decathorpe@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 31 Mar 2026 20:36:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/17] Drop vergen and don't include the git commit in the
 version

Drop the `vergen` depedency and don't include the git commit in
the return value of `rnp_version_string_full`.

For most user installations, vergen is a noop (no git repository
information available during the build).

This also drops dependencies on the `git2` and `time` crates that
are affected by RUSTSEC advisories. Migrating off the affected `git2`
version would require completely refactoring `vergen` library use
since it would require migrating to `vergen` v9. And all versions of
the `time` crate that are not affected by RUSTSEC-2026-0009 require
Rust 1.88+, which is not compatible with this project's MSRV, either.
---
